{"assumptions":["ASM-1: For this specification, “a few” sample rows means between two and five rows per empty contract-backed table."],"critic":[{"finding":"REQ-2/AC-2.5 has EnsureCreated build the schema on a database with no tables, but EnsureCreated writes no EF migrations history, so a later 'reviewed deployment migration' (AC-2.4) on that same database will try to recreate tables that already exist, and the spec never says how the two schema paths are reconciled.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":6,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-2.6 starts the new API against an older schema with a migration still pending and only checks that GET / returns 200; it never defines what contract operations return when their tables or columns don't exist yet.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-9 says to authorize 'only using the roles and scopes stated in the contract' and to add no permission table, but the anchored operations (for example createAccount and listReceipts) name no allowed roles, so the 403 path is undefined for most operations.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-9.1 depends on a 'stock collection' operation with a `warehouseId` filter, but it names no operationId and has no anchor; the only anchored collection parameters are Search, Status, DateFrom and DateTo.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-9.4 depends on 'a contract-defined password-setting operation' with no anchor, and the anchored AccountInput schema has no password field, so it is unclear whether such an operation exists.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-9.2 requires 403 for a customer reading another organization's order, while the contract lists both 403 and 404 for getCustomerOrder and nothing in the contract or the answers picks 403; that conflicts with REQ-1's 'exactly as the contract says'.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The contract's customer sign-in 'begins one-time-code verification', but the spec never says how codes are issued or delivered, or when they expire or fail, and AC-9.2 just assumes 'a valid one-time code available'.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-9 denies access to 'disabled' accounts, but no requirement says how an account becomes enabled or disabled (AccountInput has no such field), or what happens to tokens already issued to a customer whose account is then disabled.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-7.1 claims the authorization URL comes back in a response field `message`, and AC-7.3 refers vaguely to 'the response field'; neither quotes the getStaffAuthorizationUrl response schema.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-4 cites ASM-1 to fix 'a few' at two to five rows, but the accepted-assumptions list is empty, so the spec adds a constraint the human never agreed to.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":4,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-4 seeds only empty tables yet requires references to resolve to existing rows, so when a parent table already holds real data, seeded child rows would point at non-demo records; AC-4.2 also never checks the references in the tables it does seed.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-4.1's 'the rows are based on contract examples' has no observable pass/fail test, such as matching specific example field values.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-3.1 only checks that GET / returns 200 with Seed:Demo true, which tells you nothing about whether SeedData.Run actually ran.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-8.1 and AC-8.2 are near-duplicates, and neither defines what makes an identity-provider setting 'invalid' (malformed URL, unreachable issuer, missing audience), so the failure path can't be tested consistently.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-10 provisions the initial account but never says its roles or scopes, or where its email comes from, so under REQ-9's email matching it isn't clear that the first account can ever authorize admin operations.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-10.1 is a deployment 'job' check that just reads the account table, with no defined mechanism or artifact in this repo, so it can't be observed at the API surface.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-1.1 asks for every response case of every operation to be tested, including the 500 ServerError responses, which can't be triggered deliberately, so the AC can't be verified as written.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L9 size","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[],"outOfScope":["Portal screens and web-app implementation (I-5, Q-1).","Product-story behavior that is not defined by the locked OpenAPI contract (Q-1)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"Every operation and response case defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, including contract-valid and contract-invalid requests and the declared authentication and authorization cases.","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response status, content type, response fields, and error body conform to that operation's OpenAPI request and response definitions.","when":"A test client sends the corresponding HTTP requests to every declared operation."},{"given":"A caller authenticated as an account with assigned warehouse or organization 