led PostgreSQL account whose `warehouseIds` contains only 10; persisted stock rows exist in warehouses 10 and 20.","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty.","when":"The caller requests the stock collection with `warehouseId=20`."},{"given":"An existing customer account with credentials accepted by the contracted sign-in operation, a valid one-time code available for that account, an associated PostgreSQL account record assigned organization 10, and persisted orders for organizations 10 and 20.","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The sign-in and code-verification response statuses are 200, the response list contains only organization-10 records, and the response status for the organization-20 order is 403.","when":"The customer submits credentials to `POST /api/auth/customer/sign-in`, submits the issued challenge and valid code to `POST /api/auth/customer/code/verify`, then lists orders and requests an order belonging to organization 20."},{"given":"Two authenticated staff identities with associated PostgreSQL account records assigned Quality Officer and Quality Manager roles, respectively, and the same permitted quality scope; an open recall has an unaccounted quantity.","id":"AC-9.3","level":"api","then":"The Quality Officer response status is 403 and the Quality Manager response status is 200.","when":"Each account submits the contract's signed `POST /api/quality/recalls/{recallId}/write-offs` operation for that recall."},{"given":"A customer account password is set through a contract-defined password-setting operation.","id":"AC-9.4","level":"api","then":"The row's password field contains a salted password hash that verifies against the submitted password and does not equal the plaintext password.","when":"A test reads the corresponding PostgreSQL account row and verifies the stored password value against the submitted password."},{"given":"A valid staff identity-provider token has an email claim matching an enabled PostgreSQL account assigned permission to use a protected contract operation.","id":"AC-9.5","level":"api","then":"The response status is the operation's contract-declared success status.","when":"The caller sends the token with a request to that operation."},{"given":"A valid staff identity-provider token has no matching PostgreSQL account email, or matches a disabled account.","id":"AC-9.6","level":"api","then":"The response status is 403.","when":"The caller sends the token with a request to a protected contract operation."}],"anchors":[{"lineEnd":40,"lineStart":20,"path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","quote":"  /auth/customer/sign-in:\n    post:\n      operationId: signInCustomer\n      summary: \"Submit customer email and password and begin one-time-code verification.\"\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: \"#/components/schemas/Credentials\"\n      responses:\n        \"200\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/AuthResult\"\n        \"400\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/BadRequest\"\n        \"401\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\"\n        \"403\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Forbidden\"\n        \"500\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/ServerError\""},{"lineEnd":2567,"lineStart":2535,"path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","quote":"    AccountInput:\n      type: object\n      required:\n        - fullName\n        - email\n        - roles\n      properties:\n        fullName:\n          type: string\n        email:\n          type: string\n          format: email\n        roles:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: string\n            enum:\n              - Driver\n              - Dispatcher\n              - Quality Officer\n              - Quality Manager\n              - Auditor\n              - System Administrator\n              - Customer Administrator\n              - Customer\n        warehouseIds:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: integer\n        organizationIds:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            type: integer"},{"lineEnd":1685,"lineStart":1650,"path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","quote":"  /admin/accounts:\n    get:\n      operationId: listAccounts\n      summary: \"List accounts, roles and access scope.\"\n      parameters:\n        - $ref: \"#/components/parameters/Search\"\n        - $ref: \"#/components/parameters/Status\"\n      responses:\n        \"200\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Collection\"\n        \"401\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\"\n        \"403\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Forbidden\"\n        \"500\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/ServerError\"\n    post:\n      operationId: createAccount\n      summary: \"Create an account and assign its roles and access scope.\"\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: \"#/components/schemas/AccountInput\"\n      responses:\n        \"200\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/RecordResult\"\n        \"400\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/BadRequest\"\n        \"401\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\"\n        \"403\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Forbidden\"\n        \"409\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Conflict\""},{"lineEnd":1060,"lineStart":1036,"path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","quote":"  /quality/recalls/{recallId}/write-offs:\n    post:\n      operationId: writeOffRecallRemainder\n      summary: \"Submit a signed Quality Manager write-off for unaccounted recall quantity.\"\n      parameters:\n        - $ref: \"#/components/parameters/RecallId\"\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              $ref: \"#/components/schemas/WriteOffInput\"\n      responses:\n        \"200\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/RecordResult\"\n        \"400\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/BadRequest\"\n        \"401\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Unauthorized\"\n        \"403\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Forbidden\"\n        \"404\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/NotFound\"\n        \"409\":\n          $ref: \"#/components/responses/Conflict\""}],"ears":"The Meridian API shall implement customer and staff authentication and authorization only through the locked contract, store customer passwords using a standard salted password-hashing algorithm rather than as plaintext, authorize callers only using the roles and scopes stated in the contract without a separate role-to-operation permission table, match staff token email claims to enabled account emails, deny access for unmatched or disabled accounts, and add no lockout or one-time-code policies beyond the contract.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-1","Q-10","Q-11","Q-12","Q-13"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A newly deployed PostgreSQL database has no account row and the deployment has the initial account details.","id":"AC-10.1","level":"job","then":"The PostgreSQL account row list contains the provisioned initial account.","when":"The deployment provisions the initial account."}],"ears":"The Meridian deployment shall provision the initial PostgreSQL account outside the API rather than through an API bootstrap flow.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-7"],"stability":0.3333333333333333}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]},"settled":[{"decision":"How should schema changes be applied to databases that already exist when the new persistent tables are introduced? → Apply a reviewed database migration during deployment, preserving existing data; use EnsureCreated only for genuinely empty databases.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"The spec adds persistent entities but keeps startup on `EnsureCreated` (C-5), which does nothing once tables exist, and it has no migration or schema-evolution plan for existing databases despite the 'migration' risk tag.","ref":"Q-6"},{"decision":"With demo seeding disabled, how should the first PostgreSQL account be made available so the API can authorize callers? → Have deployment provision the initial account outside the API; do not add an API bootstrap flow.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"With Seed:Demo off and an empty database, no account exists, yet REQ-9 authorizes every caller from a PostgreSQL account record; the spec has no way to bootstrap the first account, and AC-5.1 assumes 'an account row provisioned by deployment' with no anchor for that process.","ref":"Q-7"},{"decision":"Which staff identity provider and concrete authorization-URL and token-validation settings should the API use? → Identify the organization's existing staff provider and supply its authorization URL and validation settings; do not introduce a new provider.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-7 has no anchors and refers to 'the existing staff identity provider', but current-behaviour shows no identity-provider integration or configuration anywhere in the codebase.","ref":"Q-8"},{"decision":"How should the test and factory runs obtain the valid nonproduction identity-provider settings required for startup? → Provide valid nonproduction settings for the chosen provider through test and factory configuration.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"Making startup fail on missing IdP settings will break the existing HealthTests.ApiIsUp and the factory runs, which supply no such settings today; REQ-7/REQ-8 claim these checks 'use valid nonproduction settings' without anchors and quietly require changing test and factory configuration.","ref":"Q-9"},{"decision":"How much customer-authentication behavior beyond the locked contract should be specified for failed logins and password storage? → Keep behavior limited to the locked contract; use standard secure password hashing for stored passwords, and do not add new lockout or one-time-code policies.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-9 has no error paths for customer authentication: wrong password, unknown email, wrong, expired or reused one-time code, and locked accounts are all missing; it also doesn't say how passwords are stored, despite the auth and pii risk tags.","ref":"Q-10"},{"decision":"Which token claim should identify the PostgreSQL staff account, and what should happen if a valid token has no matching or has a disabled account? → Match the token's email claim to the account email, and deny access when no matching enabled account exists.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-9 doesn't say how a staff IdP token maps to a PostgreSQL account record (which claim is matched), or what happens when a token is valid but has no account record, or a disabled one.","ref":"Q-11"},{"decision":"For a stock collection request whose filter names a warehouse outside the caller’s scope, what should the API return? → Return 200 OK with an empty list, applying the caller’s scope to the results.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"AC-9.1 says a stock request filtered to an out-of-scope warehouse returns 403, but AC-1.2 says scoped collection calls return a list limited to the caller's scope and the supplied filters, which implies 200 with an empty or filtered list.","ref":"Q-12"},{"decision":"Should authorization include a separate role-to-operation permission table beyond the roles and scopes stated in the locked contract? → Do not add a separate role-to-operation table; enforce only the role and scope restrictions stated by the locked contract.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-9 says callers are authorized by 'PostgreSQL account roles and scopes', but no role-to-operation permission table is given or anchored in the contract (AC-9.1 just says 'the role permitted for stock listing'), so the 403 behaviour of most operations is undefined.","ref":"Q-13"},{"decision":"How should startup determine whether a database qualifies for EnsureCreated, given that existing databases must use the reviewed deployment migration? → Use EnsureCreated only when the database has no tables; otherwise leave schema changes to the reviewed deployment migration.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-2 uses EnsureCreated for empty databases and reviewed migrations for existing ones, but EnsureCreated writes no migrations-history table, so a database it creates cannot later take a migration; the spec also never defines 'genuinely empty' or how startup detects it, even though Program.cs currently calls EnsureCreated every time.","ref":"Q-14"},{"decision":"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk","how":"open-risk","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-2/AC-2.5 has EnsureCreated build the schema on a database with no tables, but EnsureCreated writes no EF migrations history, so a later 'reviewed deployment migration' (AC-2.4) on that same database will try to recreate tables that already exist, and the spec never says how the two schema paths are reconciled."},{"decision":"Still open after 2 rounds of questions: carried as a risk","how":"open-risk","kind":"critic","problem":"REQ-9 says to authorize 'only using the roles and scopes stated in the contract' and to add no permission table, but the anchored operations (for example createAccount and listReceipts) name no allowed roles, so the 403 path is undefined for most operations."}]}